% tst_zerndef_fringe.in -- PLAN_CONSOLIDATION item 7 (Dave 2026-10-10): every
% Zernike-carrying surface defaults to ZernType= ANSI whatever its element
% type.  An NS Cassegrain (= tst_zrngr_roundtrip.in) whose primary is a
% Surface= ZrnGrData with NO grid declared (cwd-independent; the grid term is
% inert), ZernCoef mode 9 = 2e-7 m, no nZernCoef=, and ZernType= Fringe.
% GATE (cli_tests/cmd/ZernType_default.jou): the none and ansi twins trace to
% the IDENTICAL OPD; the fringe twin differs (mode 9 = spherical in Fringe,
% trefoil in ANSI).  Pre-change the none twin loads but its ZrnGrData kept
% ZernTypeL 0 (the Zernike default is pre-empted at Surface= for any type
% but Zernike), so its coefficients never reached the trace -- the red.
        ChfRayDir=  0.0E+00  0.0E+00  1.0E+00
        ChfRayPos=  0.0E+00  0.0E+00  -5.0E+00
          zSource=1.0E+21

